-- EntityDefinition — a user-defined entity type: schema + default render
-- templates.
--
-- Static rows: none. Lives in the dedicated `types` SQL table —
-- registered here purely for the validation surface. Identity is lifted
-- from the directives below; the auto-register loop registers it. The
-- pre-flip inline-TS `defineSystemEntity` is GONE.
--
-- typed-function-references Phase 9a / 9a-4 — `name` / `label` /
-- `description` have ALL collapsed OUT of this $record into typeclass
-- instances (Codeable / Labelable / Describable) keyed by the type's
-- name (the universal codeName thesis: identity + display are projections
-- keyed by the target id, not schema fields). They were already absent
-- from the `types` table columns (dropped in unified-dispatch Phase 6);
-- `types.name` stays the persistence KEY, sourced OUTSIDE the validated
-- schema (the POST /types path reads `name` off the raw body before
-- validateBody). So author ONLY the 3 surviving fields — do NOT re-add
-- the collapsed ones. See the comment ladder at the deleted
-- defineSystemEntity for the full history.
--
-- FM-retire-E1 Step 6 — id ships LOWERCASE via `@codeName "entity_definition"`.
-- `type: Maybe ({})` needs parens (compound `{}` arg, see integration.fenel).

@entity
@codeName "entity_definition"
@label "Entity Definition"
@description "User-defined entity type — name + schema + default render templates"
@icon "type-set"
EntityDefinition = EntityDefinition type: Maybe ({}) defaultTemplate: Maybe String defaultTemplateInline: Maybe String
